The legal text comes from the Constitutional Council of Lebanon (https://www.cc.gov.lb), the Constitution, Arabic text, retrieved on 29 October 2026. The Council states no licence for the legal texts. They are official legal texts; their copyright status is not confirmed here, and they are reproduced with the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; footnotes, running heads and page numbers were removed; and the text was arranged as git commits. The wording of the law was not changed. The Constitutional Council of Lebanon does not endorse this repository.

The codes listed in the README are official legislation published by the Legal Informatics Center of the Lebanese University (https://legiliban.ul.edu.lb), which states no licence for them; they are reproduced with this attribution. The Lebanese University does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
